            {
                "entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                "word": "purdah",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "06163488-d690-4722-a088-8051ee1bb184",
                        "entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "purdahs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "750f066e-45e8-3ccd-9bb7-b8cdad6e9955",
                        "entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Dans le sous-continent indien et dans des pays où domine la religion musulmane, pratique sociale de séparation stricte entre les hommes et les femmes, qui doivent échapper aux regards masculins."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1176eaf9-0726-492d-b64e-d6519b8c934c",
                                "sense_id": "750f066e-45e8-3ccd-9bb7-b8cdad6e9955",
                                "text": "Dans les rues étroites et fraîches de cette vieille ville, nous n’avions pas vu une seule femme ; et bien sûr, pas davantage au café… Le purdah d’Italie semblait aussi strict que celui de Kaboul."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50932c9a-a77e-4c22-b3d0-54051f969cc0",
                                "sense_id": "750f066e-45e8-3ccd-9bb7-b8cdad6e9955",
                                "text": "Dans l’Orient contemporain, où beaucoup de femmes ne vivent plus le purdah dans le sens original du terme, c’est-à-dire cloîtrées dans les quartiers féminins de la maison, il s’est transformé en un ensemble de limitations implicites bâtissant un mur invisible séparant l’homme de la femme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fffb9c0f-12cd-4cd0-9e5e-9236f49838a3",
                                "sense_id": "750f066e-45e8-3ccd-9bb7-b8cdad6e9955",
                                "text": "Pour l’Aga Khan, le système du purdah ne trouve de justification ni dans le Coran ni dans la Sunna."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57c7212f-edcf-42a8-92a9-ea6f1120bd02",
                                "sense_id": "750f066e-45e8-3ccd-9bb7-b8cdad6e9955",
                                "text": "- La purdah n’est pas un privilège, mais une vie de restrictions, poursuivit Vandana avec simplicité. La maharani peut voyager à quelques kilomètres pour prier au temple familial - mais quand elle s’y rend, son palanquin doit être fermé par des rideaux. Personne ne doit voir son visage."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b98cc674-dfda-3ce7-9a77-8e4bf904940b",
                        "entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Rideau, tenture, paravent destiné à établir cette séparation, à cacher les présences féminines."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aac9a94-2828-4fb1-9b49-7a93a4697494",
                                "sense_id": "b98cc674-dfda-3ce7-9a77-8e4bf904940b",
                                "text": "Nous étions à peu de distance de la Begum ; mais des purdahs épais nous ôtaient l’espoir de jeter un seul coup d’œil au-dedans."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a895394b-cb1e-30cd-8a87-231aff3a3e32",
                        "entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Voile féminin grillagé au niveau des yeux, assimilable à la burqa."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65672fcb-53df-465f-bb94-029fed355434",
                                "sense_id": "a895394b-cb1e-30cd-8a87-231aff3a3e32",
                                "text": "Les Musulmanes déambulaient cachées sous leurs purdahs, voiles de claustration blancs, verts, même noirs, incrustés à la hauteur du nez d’une fenêtre en dentelle qui laissait passer leurs sombres regards."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "acf6b924-0427-4b3d-950c-446efcfa60db",
                        "source_entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "source_sense_description": "pratique sociale",
                        "target_lang_word": "Parda",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "011f3a37-5459-4eff-8705-a6e7da2212a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "917e773c-a4ed-351d-8046-96d617ee961c",
                        "source_sense_description": "pratique sociale",
                        "target_lang_word": "purdah",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "purdah",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e926751-0941-3e01-b7a2-26908389d232",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curtain, especially one used in some Hindu or Muslim traditions to conceal women from the gaze of people, particularly men and strangers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "South-Asia",
                                            "also",
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ecccc3ad-1f9d-4dd7-824d-eaa8c11808df",
                                                "sense_id": "7e926751-0941-3e01-b7a2-26908389d232",
                                                "text": "As she passed through the dining-room she heard, behind the purdah that cloaked the drawing-room door, her husband's voice, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "145c5acf-7131-4335-8d90-47fe2044f916",
                                                "sense_id": "7e926751-0941-3e01-b7a2-26908389d232",
                                                "text": "\"Come and see my wife a little then,\" said Hamidullah, and they spent twenty minutes behind the purdah."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d04d676c-98ae-30c9-a208-7970978cdf57",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A long veil or other attire covering most of the body, worn by women in some Muslim societies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef4c5942-8b43-30dd-b6be-145c85333b12",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The situation or system of secluding women from the gaze of people, particularly men and strangers, in some Muslim and Hindu traditions, by using a curtain or screen, and/or wearing a face veil or attire covering most of the body."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9be68375-0985-4ab3-8d0a-4b3113245033",
                                                "sense_id": "ef4c5942-8b43-30dd-b6be-145c85333b12",
                                                "text": "He was won by her love for him, by a loyalty that implied something more than submission, and by her efforts to educate herself against that lifting of the purdah that would come in the next generation if not in theirs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "219749c6-fdf5-39fb-90cd-81b4f6819acb",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Keeping apart; isolation, seclusion; also, concealment, secrecy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bff9c3d-24ad-4742-bb5b-4da7d1c540be",
                                                "sense_id": "219749c6-fdf5-39fb-90cd-81b4f6819acb",
                                                "text": "The diagnosis of Kit's malady was soon verified, and Fleur went into purdah."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21a945c0-b2ab-4fe4-a9d7-b14bd12b7d62",
                                                "sense_id": "219749c6-fdf5-39fb-90cd-81b4f6819acb",
                                                "text": "Still, though the lettrist movement was not casual—members might be fined, put in purdah, or even expelled for malingering—aesthetic pluralism remained in effect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca01c77c-9e31-3f1b-9305-03124f4022a9",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The period between the announcement of an election or referendum and its conclusion, during which civil servants refrain from making policy announcements or taking actions that could be seen as advantageous to certain candidates in the election."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6571536c-c923-408c-ace8-fb80580b0a45",
                                                "sense_id": "ca01c77c-9e31-3f1b-9305-03124f4022a9",
                                                "text": "Despite Rail Minister Chris Heaton-Harris's reassurance that \"the White Paper is coming\" it was further delayed by the period of purdah that preceded local elections held on May 6."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bfa18c81-a54c-32e3-adb4-ebb33bd09afa",
                                        "entry_id": "42fdc1ce-906d-3753-8adf-bc8c248a3e79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A striped cotton cloth which is used to make curtains."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "rare",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
